# M3.5.2 server inventory diagnostic — 2026-08-27

## Trigger

The first strictly read-only inventory command assumed `rg` was installed on
`ubuntu-8gb-nbg1-2`. The server returned `rg: command not found`. No write or
runtime action had occurred.

## Cause and controlled fallback

The workstation has ripgrep; the server image does not. The inventory was
stopped at that command and repeated with read-only `grep` and `find`. Future
server preflight scripts must use POSIX tools or explicitly test optional tool
availability before use.

## Result

- Tailscale-only SSH to `chatops@100.121.130.51` passed.
- Control is clean at `30d5e139ec50b2332cf5aea3bfc5ad4c4c95fcfa`.
- Adult Core is clean but stale at `5572ea165c11fa9d409d1e76ddf08243ae657ea0`;
  remote `main` is `dddb94e8ac3d79f6ccd7d696d2fa92da1583850b`.
- No Docker mount or inspected service write path targets the planned immutable
  release root.
- `lsof +D` showed no application-path handles, but unprivileged Docker
  overlay/netns warnings prevent treating that particular check as complete.
  This item remains HOLD until a privileged, approved activation preflight.
- No files, services, timers, containers, credentials, or network rules were
  changed.

## Decision

Read-only planning may continue. Server activation remains prohibited.
